WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.847
Responsible use starts before inference.

00:00:02.847 --> 00:00:07.962
First ask whether the data is appropriate to send to the selected model or service.

00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:16.657
Remove or protect sensitive information when required, and understand the provider or local deployment policy.

00:00:16.657 --> 00:00:20.417
Next, identify what kind of error would matter most for the task.

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:26.917
A false positive in spam filtering is different from an unsupported claim in a medical or legal setting.

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:32.207
Evaluate with representative data rather than a few convenient examples.

00:00:32.207 --> 00:00:37.092
Keep track of the exact checkpoint, tokenizer, configuration, prompt,

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:41.742
and software versions so results can be reproduced.

00:00:41.742 --> 00:00:44.282
Review the model card and license.

00:00:44.282 --> 00:00:49.682
Monitor performance after deployment because real input can differ from development data.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:56.487
And when a system produces factual claims, connect outputs to verifiable evidence whenever possible.

00:00:56.487 --> 00:01:04.142
Responsible NLP is not one checkbox; it is a process that continues from model selection through evaluation

00:01:04.142 --> 00:01:04.839
and deployment.
